  "atomic_rules": [
    "Reserve a complete nonnegative exact-int charge under one lock before any mutation of reference-bearing structures. Reject if n>limit-used, without incrementing.",
    "The allocation lock protects instrumentation only. Never hold it across the original callable, domain I/O, waits or cleanup; preserve original synchronization and calls.",
    "A reservation commits exactly once when all candidate rows pass existing field/byte/value checks. On failure, the whole reference-bearing mutation must be absent; previously committed evidence remains. Do not rollback counts already committed or reuse an allocated public identity.",
    "Allocation capacity and raw/table byte growth are preflighted jointly. Generic owner/observer paths also need coverage; replacing only reference() after a structure mutation is insufficient.",
    "First fault latches; original callable executes exactly once with original return/exception identity. Cleanup/restoration completes through existing paths; capture is invalid, no auto retry.",
    "Diagnostic stays in the existing4096-byte allowlisted envelope and first phase/code; fixed aggregate resource summary may be inline in normal context only if encoded within current caps, never a bypass counter or new channel.",
    "Reader recomputes graph membership/headers/context and validates committed counts with source/certificate; favorable resource numbers do not waive semantic missing evidence."
  ],
